  "scope": "Bridge the existing FAULT_N left main group to the existing lower-right protection group. This does not close all FAULT_N pins.",
  "copper": "17 segments, width 0.20 mm, total added length 32.826119 mm; one 0.50/0.30 mm through via at (32.2,29.0). No old copper, placements, padstacks, rules or keepouts changed.",
  "mounted_face_escape": "Both ends reuse existing FAULT_N vias. The new B route follows the free corridor between header pin rows; it crosses no B component body guard. The In3 approach uses a 45-degree entry to the exact retained destination via center, avoiding R127A off-center termination.",
  "reference": "B.Cu and In3.Cu both use In4.Cu. Native filled ground covers every added stroke outside its own terminal/transfer lands and clearance voids. No new reference transition flags; seven historical flags remain. New via does not reduce retained-trace reference coverage or old power/GND connectivity.",
