      "route_layers": [
        "B.Cu",
        "In3.Cu"
      ],
      "body_face": "F.Cu",
      "review": "New routes project under sections of the front-side MCU header. Native mounted-face/through-via prohibitions remain intact. The adjacent In4 reference stays continuous along the new strokes outside own transfer voids; no buck/SW, Kelvin or thermal-power component is newly crossed by this bridge. Header-signal crosstalk and loaded FAULT_N transient behavior still need whole-board electrical/bench review; DRC is not their qualification."
    }
  ],
  "thermal": "No heat-generating component, power current route or dissipation is changed. Header and board installed thermal/assembly qualification remain outstanding.",
  "alternatives": "R127A connects the same groups but has a native endpoint-not-centered warning; not adopted. The 0.05-mm fixed-placement search proposed a similar roughly 32.18-mm bridge with a different via; it did not connect the other isolated FAULT_N ends. The validated R127B has 17 explicit segments and no added regression loss; bounded search results are not an impossibility proof.",
